1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:01,960
IN 1962,

2
00:00:01,960 --> 00:00:03,180
A MAN LIVED IN A CAVE

3
00:00:03,180 --> 00:00:04,316
WITH NO CLOCKS.

4
00:00:04,616 --> 00:00:06,311
HE LOST 25 DAYS.

5
00:00:06,761 --> 00:00:07,978
A FRENCH SCIENTIST WENT

6
00:00:07,978 --> 00:00:09,260
130 METRES

7
00:00:09,260 --> 00:00:10,500
UNDERGROUND.

8
00:00:10,500 --> 00:00:12,440
NO WATCH. NO SUN.

9
00:00:12,440 --> 00:00:13,080
HE SLEPT WHEN

10
00:00:13,080 --> 00:00:14,199
HIS BODY SAID SO.

11
00:00:14,500 --> 00:00:15,560
HIS TEAM ASKED HIM

12
00:00:15,560 --> 00:00:17,660
TO COUNT TO 120,

13
00:00:17,660 --> 00:00:18,980
ONE NUMBER A SECOND.

14
00:00:18,980 --> 00:00:19,560
IT TOOK HIM

15
00:00:19,560 --> 00:00:20,531
FIVE MINUTES.

16
00:00:22,716 --> 00:00:23,940
WHEN HIS TEAM CALLED TIME

17
00:00:23,940 --> 00:00:25,760
ON 14 SEPTEMBER,

18
00:00:25,760 --> 00:00:26,420
HE THOUGHT IT WAS

19
00:00:26,420 --> 00:00:27,658
20 AUGUST.

20
00:00:28,108 --> 00:00:28,600
BUT HIS BODY

21
00:00:28,600 --> 00:00:30,280
NEVER LOST THE BEAT.

22
00:00:30,280 --> 00:00:31,500
BY HIS OWN COUNT,

23
00:00:31,500 --> 00:00:32,573
HIS DAYS RAN ABOUT

24
00:00:32,573 --> 00:00:34,378
24½ HOURS.

25
00:00:34,720 --> 00:00:35,380
LATER, HARVARD

26
00:00:35,380 --> 00:00:36,860
SPOTTED A CATCH.

27
00:00:36,860 --> 00:00:38,340
IN ISOLATION EXPERIMENTS

28
00:00:38,340 --> 00:00:39,160
LIKE THESE,

29
00:00:39,160 --> 00:00:40,460
SWITCHING ON A LAMP

30
00:00:40,460 --> 00:00:41,631
RESETS THE CLOCK.

31
00:00:42,040 --> 00:00:43,180
MEASURED PROPERLY,

32
00:00:43,180 --> 00:00:44,184
YOUR INTERNAL DAY IS

33
00:00:44,184 --> 00:00:45,240
24 HOURS

34
00:00:45,240 --> 00:00:46,647
AND 11 MINUTES.

35
00:00:50,353 --> 00:00:51,440
HE LOST COUNT.

36
00:00:51,440 --> 00:00:52,501
HIS BODY DIDN'T.

